  "comment": "audit/dotenv-interoperability: every external implementation the census runs, pinned. Libraries are pinned by their ecosystem's own lock (oracles/*: package-lock.json, requirements*.txt with hashes, Gemfile.lock with CHECKSUMS, packages.lock.json in locked mode) or, where the ecosystem has none (Java, the Node runtime), by the artifact's SHA-256 here. tools/setup.py installs everything into the census cache and refuses an artifact whose digest differs; tools/setup.py check-latest compares the pins with the registries. Runtimes the CI host provides (Bash, Python, Ruby, the JDK) are asserted, not installed: a run on another version is refused unless --any-runtime is given, and every result records the version that produced it.",
